rritory of Christmas Island\n\nconventional short form: Christmas Island","ordinal":37,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:37","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Dependency status","content":"non-self governing territory of Australia; administered from Canberra by the Australian Department of Transport and Regional Services","ordinal":38,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:38","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Government type","content":"NA","ordinal":39,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:39","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Capital","content":"name: The Settlement\n\ngeographic coordinates: 10 25 S, 105 43 E\n\ntime difference: UTC+7 (12 hours ahead of Washington, DC during Standard Time)","ordinal":40,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:40","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"none (territory of Australia)","ordinal":41,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:41","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (territory of Australia)","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:42","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Australia Day, 26 January (1788)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:43","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"Christmas Island Act of 1958-59 (1 October 1958) as amended by the Territories Law Reform Act of 1992","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:44","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"under the authority of the governor general of Australia and Australian law","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:45","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952), represented by the Australian governor general\n\nhead of government: Administrator Neil LUCAS (since 30 January 2006)\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; administrator appointed by the governor general of Australia and represents the monarch and Australia","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:46","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Christmas Island Shire Council (9 seats; members elected by popular vote to serve four-year terms)\n\nelections: held every two years with half the members standing for election; last held 20 October 2007 (next to be held in 2009)\n\nelection results: percent of vote - NA; seats - independents 9","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:47","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Supreme Court; District Court; Magistrate's Court","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:48","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"none","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:49","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"none","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:50","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"none","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:51","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (territory of Australia)","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:52","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (territory of Australia)","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:53","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"territorial flag; divided diagonally from upper hoist to lower fly; the upper triangle is green with a yellow image of the Golden Bosun Bird superimposed, while the lower triangle is blue with the Southern Cross constellation, representing Australia, superimposed; a centered yellow disk displays a green map of the island; the flag of Australia is used for official purposes","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:54","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Phosphate mining had been the only significant economic activity, but in December 1987 the Australian Government closed the mine. In 1991, the mine was reopened. With the support of the government, a $34 million casino opened in 1993, but closed in 1998. The Australian Government in 2001 agreed to support the creation of a commercial space-launching site on the island, expected to begin operations in the near future.","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:55","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$NA","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:56","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"NA","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:57","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Budget","content":"revenues: $NA\n\nexpenditures: $NA","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:58","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Agriculture - products","content":"NA","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/kt.html#field:59","country":"CX","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Industries","content